Inspect and recover Chab operations.

Operation starts create a private local action record before sending the first
effectful request. The action record stores recovery metadata and an
idempotency key, but never stores a bearer token or request body.
Journal directories are created private where the platform supports file
permissions. Record writes sync the data file before atomic publication;
directory metadata sync is best effort for portability.

Schemas are read from the pinned Chab API contract embedded in the binary, so
schema inspection works offline.

Related commands:
  chab search web
  chab credits balance

Usage:
  chab operations [flags]
  chab operations [command]

Available Commands:
  actions     Inspect local action records
  artifact    Fetch operation artifact metadata
  bulk-cancel Cancel operations by filter
  cancel      Cancel an operation
  estimate    Estimate an operation request
  list        List remote operations
  result      Fetch operation result metadata
  resume      Resume a local action
  schema      Show an embedded operation schema
  show        Show operation status
  start       Start a supported operation by key
  wait        Wait for an operation to finish

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for operations

Global Flags:
      --api-base-url string   API base URL (Chab default uses www.chab.ai/v1; custom base URLs use <base-url>/v1)
      --auth-file string      path to the CLI auth file
      --base-url string       product web base URL
      --config string         path to the CLI config file
      --debug                 write redacted request details to stderr
      --include-meta          include safe response metadata in machine output where supported
      --jq string             filter supported JSON output with a jq expression
      --json                  print stable JSON output where supported
      --locale string         response language sent as Accept-Language (en or de)
      --no-ansi               disable ANSI terminal controls and paging where supported
      --no-color              disable color in human output where supported
      --no-pager              disable pager use for long human output where supported
      --no-prompt             fail instead of prompting for interactive input
      --plain                 print copy-safe plain output where supported
      --profile string        profile to use for this invocation
      --template string       render supported JSON output with a Go text/template
      --yes                   accept supported confirmations for risky or destructive operations; does not supply missing input

Use "chab operations [command] --help" for more information about a command.
